config VIDEO_EXYNOS_ISPFE
	bool "Google zumapro ISPFE camera receive complex"
	depends on ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF
	depends on PM
	help
	  Bring-up driver for BLK_ISPFE on Google's zumapro (Tensor G4): the
	  CSIS links and their combo D/C-PHYs, the ISPFE front end, and the
	  PDMA that carries per-frame descriptors.

	  At this stage the driver powers the block, restores the CMU state that
	  the power domain does not, and provides debugfs controls for a captured
	  sensor mode.  It registers no V4L2 devices and is of no use outside
	  camera bring-up.

	  This is built-in because module removal cannot be aborted if the shared
	  PHY isolation fails to restore before the ISPFE power domain goes down.

	  If unsure, say N.
